png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l24ljxen/43e98227-0517-4266-9ad9-d9b54c54a4c7/793486f0-bf05-11ec-8fbf-67f2639a0a45/file-1l24ljxeo.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2012 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Aldehydes, Ketones and Carboxylic Acids Question 38 English\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l24ljxen/43e98227-0517-4266-9ad9-d9b54c54a4c7/793486f0-bf05-11ec-8fbf-67f2639a0a45/file-1l24ljxeo.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l24ljxen/43e98227-0517-4266-9ad9-d9b54c54a4c7/793486f0-bf05-11ec-8fbf-67f2639a0a45/file-1l24ljxeo.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l24ljxen/43e98227-0517-4266-9ad9-d9b54c54a4c7/793486f0-bf05-11ec-8fbf-67f2639a0a45/file-1l24ljxeo.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l24ljxen/43e98227-0517-4266-9ad9-d9b54c54a4c7/793486f0-bf05-11ec-8fbf-67f2639a0a45/file-1l24ljxeo.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l24ljxen/43e98227-0517-4266-9ad9-d9b54c54a4c7/793486f0-bf05-11ec-8fbf-67f2639a0a45/file-1l24ljxeo.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l24ljxen/43e98227-0517-4266-9ad9-d9b54c54a4c7/793486f0-bf05-11ec-8fbf-67f2639a0a45/file-1l24ljxeo.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"C<sub>6</sub>H<sub>5</sub>OH and C<sub>6</sub>H<sub>5</sub>COOH"},{"identifier":"B","content":"C<sub>6</sub>H<sub>5</sub>COOH and C<sub>6</sub>H<sub>5</sub>CH<sub>2</sub>OH"},{"identifier":"C","content":"C<sub>6</sub>H<sub>5</sub>CH<sub>2</sub>OH and C<sub>6</sub>H<sub>5</sub>OH"},{"identifier":"D","content":"C<sub>6</sub>H<sub>5</sub>CH<sub>2</sub>OH and C<sub>6</sub>H<sub>5</sub>CH<sub>2</sub>COOH"}],"correct_options":["B","D"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p>Both phenol and benzoic acid are soluble in NaOH, so they cannot be separated.</p>\n<p>C<sub>6</sub>H<sub>5</sub>OH + NaOH <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.181ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -511 1000 522\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2192\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2192\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> C<sub>6</sub>H<sub>5</sub>ONa + H<sub>2</sub>O</p>\n<p>C<sub>6</sub>H<sub>5</sub>COOH + NaOH <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.181ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -511 1000 522\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2192\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2192\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> C<sub>6</sub>H<sub>5</sub>COONa + H<sub>2</sub>O</p>\n<p>Benzel alcohol C<sub>6</sub>H<sub>5</sub>CH<sub>2</sub>OH is not soluble in NaOH and NaHCO<sub>3</sub>, while benzoic acid is soluble in both, so these can be separated. Both C<sub>6</sub>H<sub>5</sub>OH and C<sub>6</sub>H<sub>5</sub>CH<sub>2</sub>OH are insoluble in NaHCO<sub>3</sub>, so they cannot be separated. C<sub>6</sub>H<sub>5</sub>CH<sub>2</sub>COOH is soluble in NaOH and NaHCO<sub>3</sub>, whereas benzyl alcohol is not soluble in NaOH and NaHCO<sub>3</sub>. So, they can be separated.</p>"}},"subject":"chemistry","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":180000,"topic":"preparation-properties-and-uses-of-carboxylic-acids","type":"mcqm","year":2012,"isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"yearKey":"iit-jee-2012-paper-1-offline","active":true}],"ids":["1l23l4epy","1l23l5xu9","1l23lae0b","1l23lg413"],"title":"IIT-JEE 2012 Paper 1 Offline | JEE Advanced Year Wise Previous Years Questions","canonical":"https://app/past-years/jee/pthe-colour-of-light-absorbed-by-an-aqueous-solution-of-cu-jee-advanced-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-mziys50tu256jetn"}